Note:
    The playable game now lives in ../dungeon.bas (a vertical slice assembling the
    scratchpad prototypes). Items below are checked off against that build.

Roadmap (future / bigger efforts):
    ✔ Extract a REUSABLE ENGINE from the game @done(26-07-29)
        DONE and verified -- engine/ names NO game symbol; every engine->game call goes
        through one of 11 Game_* hooks. engine/ is also self-contained on disk (the
        vendored ansi/ renderer + the DICE3D module moved in), so the directory can be
        lifted out as-is. include/ now holds only the reference submodules.
        The authority is engine/ENGINE.md (layout, hook contract, how each leak closed).
        ✔ engine/  -- BOARD CURSOR MUSIC JUICE GESTURE STATS DATA UI ARTPACK SAVEIO
          MARKDOWN TEXT + ansi/ + DICE3D/ + DICE3D_GAME.
        ✔ game/   -- HOOKS OVERLAYS LOADERS CHAMBERS MANIFEST DEBUG PLAYERS COMBAT PLAY
          MENU SPRITES SECTOR SOLO FLAVOR CTEXT CURIO EFFECTS SAVEGAME CHRONICLE LORDS.
        ✔ DUNGEON.BI split per-declaration into engine/ENGINE.BI + game/GAME.BI.
        ✔ PROVEN, not just asserted: examples/minimal is a second game on engine/ alone
          (no game/ at all) that walks a player around the board in ~50 lines of hooks.
          Building it immediately exposed a real bug -- see the DetectDoors note below.
        ✔ ENFORCED by scripts, not discipline (tests/run-tests.sh runs all of these):
            audit-boundary.sh      no engine/ file may name a game/ symbol; also checks
                                   every hook the engine CALLS is DEFINED by both games
            audit-shadow.sh        no local named after a high-risk shared global
            audit-shortcircuit.sh  no bounds guard relying on short-circuit (QB64 has none)
            6 unit suites          200 assertions over the game-free engine modules
        ✔ BUG FOUND BY THE ABOVE: DetectDoors counted hits in a local named `brown`,
          which case-insensitively shadowed the shared BROWN colour -- so it compared each
          pixel against the counter (0) and found ZERO doors, forever. MarkStrongDoors
          marked nothing and reinforced doors never once appeared in play. Fixed; 192 doors
          now detected, ~1 in 6 reinforced as the rules intend.
        ✔ Also hardened: TokLoad crashed on a missing save (_READFILE$ errors rather than
          returning ""); StatAppend now rotates a stale CSV aside on schema drift.
        ~ NOT done, and deliberately: hooks #3/#4/#9-#15 remain inlined in dungeon.bas.
          That file is the ASSEMBLY and is allowed to name both sides -- lifting them would
          make dungeon.bas reusable too, which no one needs yet. Not debt.

    ☐ DEEP TACTICAL COMBAT screen (party vs. a group of enemies -- see mockup):
        REFERENCE MOCKUP: assets/ansi/ui-fight.xb  (XBIN, editable in text mode -- the
          full screen layout the mockup shows). Supporting art already made:
          assets/ansi/monsters/gnoll.xb (+.ans/.icy) enemy portrait,
          assets/ansi/dice/d20.xb (+.ans/.icy) die art. Render/edit the .xb in an
          XBIN editor (DRAW / PabloDraw); the .ans variants can be ANSI_Print'd in-game.
        A full Gold-Box/Darkest-Dungeon-style encounter screen. Big evolution of
        DoCombatDnD. Reuses what we have: HpBar$, the dice tumbler/pip dice, crit
        detection + "CRITICAL HIT!" fanfare, per-actor HP / to-hit / AC / damage die.
        New systems it needs:
        ☐ Multi-enemy encounters -- fight a GROUP at once (e.g. 4 gnolls), each an
          actor with its own portrait, weapon (mace 1d6, spear 1d4, claw 1d2...),
          armour/AC, and HP bar. (Ties into CHAMBERS below.)
        ☐ Initiative + turn order bar ("ROUND n / INITIATIVE: GNOLL1 > PLAYER > ...")
          with the active actor highlighted; cycle turns.
        ☐ Health TIERS derived from HP% (WOUNDED / BLOODIED / CRITICAL / AT DEATH'S DOOR)
        ☐ Stances (ATTACKING / GUARDING / PRONE) affecting to-hit / defence
        ☐ Status effects with duration -- POISONED -1 (3/3), PRONE, etc. (tick per round)
        ☐ Action menu: ATTACK (melee/ranged) - GUARD - CAST - USE - FLEE, with target
          selection (crosshair over the chosen enemy)
        ☐ Spells (the Dungeon! Spell Cards): Lightning Bolt, Fireball, Heal, ...
        ☐ Persistent scrolling COMBAT LOG (to-hit rolls, damage, effects) -- extend ScrollText
        ☐ Combat STATS counters -- PLAYER (left) vs MONSTER (right) columns showing
          # CRITS / # FUMBLES / # MAX DAMAGE / TOTAL DAMAGE.  [requested 2026-07-27]
          (chronicle already tracks g_crits/g_fumbles for the player; extend to the
          monster side + a max-damage tally + running total, drawn on the combat
          panel -- see DrawCombatPanel / DUNGEON! FX_* combat context.)
        ☐ Crit fanfare with narrated consequences ("entrails fly", "slammed prone", bonus
          damage shown: 1d8(+1) = 7 x2 = 14)
        ☐ Enemy + player PORTRAITS (ANSI art per monster / class)
        ☐ Colour-coded polyhedral dice tray (d20/d12/d10/d8/d6/d4) -- extend the tumbler
        This is the flagship consumer of the reusable engine's combat subsystem.

    ☐ Special rooms = CHAMBERS with elaborate encounters (Darkest-Dungeon-style):
        Per the manual, Dungeon! Rooms hold 1 monster + 1 treasure; CHAMBERS hold a
        3-monster gauntlet and NO treasure (only dropped loot), and allow multiple
        pawns. Build on the existing room detection:
        ☐ Tag room-blocks as ROOM vs CHAMBER (the named big ones = chambers)
        ☐ Rooms keep 1-monster + treasure; Chambers run a 3-monster gauntlet
        ☐ Chamber EVENT table: gauntlet, curios (shrine/altar risk-reward choices),
          traps/hazards, and "LORD" random events (scripted encounters)

