Refinement backlog (from playtest 26-07-24):
    ✔ Level Key hidden on a random DEEP level (never level 1); Crystal Ball pinpoints the room @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Default settings match the player's config (D&D, 4d6-drop, Sapphire, slow dice, slow combat, smooth) @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Wandering monsters from LINGERING (loiter meter): searches / long idle spawn a random @done(26-07-24)
      encounter of the CURRENT level. `loiter` global reset per game.
        ✔ Escalating ATMOSPHERIC HINTS before the encounter fires (LoiterOmen$: subtle omens, @done(26-07-24)
          then close, then the fight). Two pools: subtle -> close.
    ✔ Dice PHYSICS: full 3D physics via the DICE3D module -- gravity, wall/floor bounce, tumbling @done(26-07-25)
      rotation, and settle-into-a-row. Far exceeds the original font-approach plan (real polyhedra).
    ~ LEGENDARY LORDS overhaul: per-level progression (levels 1-9 reached), monsters killed and gold
      earned PER LEVEL are now CAPTURED in the v2 save (lvl_reached/lvl_kills/lvl_gold/lvl_cleared).
      REMAINING: the viewer UI -- select a lord to see their full per-level character sheet.
    ☐ Treasure/ITEM CARD drops per the DUNGEON! rules: verify the item deck + drop odds against the
      manual (Magic Sword, Magic Bow/Arrow, Shield, Cloak, ESP Medallion, Crystal Ball, Elf Boots,
      Teleport, Wizard spells, etc.) and their per-level frequency; expand TRE_ITEM beyond the current 5.
    ~ To-hit is class base + attribute mod (STR fighters / INT wizard) -- e.g. Hero +7 = +4 class +3 STR;
      shown by CombatDerivation$. Working as designed; revisit class base values if combat stays too easy.

Refinement-2 backlog (from live playtest 26-07-24 -- see REFINEMENT-2-REVIEW.md):
    ✔ FIX: monster markers landed on walls (L-shaped rooms) so combat never fired @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Healing potions: treasure 50% (1d8), level-clear cache (1d4 + 30% 1d8), [H] to quaff @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ XP + D&D leveling: XP per kill; clearing a floor levels you up + rolls a hit die for HP @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Item progression: swords/armor always logged + each find one step stronger (capped) @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Crit/fumble effects ENGINE (data-driven EFFECTS.bas): crit cinematic + heal, player fumble,
      monster natural-1 self-hit/lose-turn; SETTINGS "Crits & Fumbles" toggle @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Monster natural-1 hits itself / loses a turn; hero natural-20 double damage @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Curio chests after fights (20%), 25% trapped: poison darts / bomb / frost bomb / magic siren,
      each with a CON/DEX/WIS saving throw; poison+fire DoT, frost no-move, siren +encounters @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Status effects tick per step + shown in the HUD @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ HUD: turn/move count, character level, potion count, status readout, per-player DEATHS @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Hardcore idle mode (SETTINGS "Time Passes When Idle"); casual = idling safe @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Cleared levels safe; secret-door rooms are sanctuaries once cleared; lean wander loot @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Monsters hidden until their room is ENTERED (even FOV off); never drawn on level labels @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Loot recovery (SETTINGS toggle, default D&D on): death leaves loot in the room to reclaim @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ ESP Medallion foresees the monster beyond a door ([Y] enter / [N] back off) @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Character creation: press-key-to-roll each stat + [A] auto; show class bonuses; random funny names @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Combat stats CSV log (dungeon-stats.csv) for difficulty analysis @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Save / load game (single slot, seed-reproduced) + [G] save + CONTINUE on entry @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ [P] pause for bio breaks; death waits for a keypress before the blood transition @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Dice ROTATION: polyhedra spin via _MAPTRIANGLE (render die to scratch image, rotate-blit, ease
      upright on settle). Verified via scratchpads/TEST-DICE-ROT.bas. @done(26-07-24)
    ✔ Multiplayer save/load @done(26-07-29) -- save v5 adds a PLRS block holding every
      hot-seat seat, so [G] now works in multiplayer (was solo-only). SaveGame syncs the
      ACTIVE seat first (its state lives in the working globals and is only parked on a turn
      change). Player names are written with spaces encoded as CHR$(1) -- the loader splits on
      whitespace, so "Grognard the Fast" would otherwise become 3 tokens and desync the whole
      positional stream. Verified by `dungeon.run savetest`, which round-trips 4 synthetic seats
      AND loads a copy of the real save to prove the bump did not orphan it.
    ✔ Per-player inventory gap @done(26-07-29) -- FIXED. The PLAYER record gained the 15
      remaining per-seat fields (armour, shield, bow, boots, teleport, both potions, both spell
      charges, char level + XP, and the four status timers), Load/SaveActivePlayer park and
      restore them, and save v6 persists them. Before this, passing the turn did NOT swap them:
      every hot-seat player shared one inventory, one XP total and one poison timer.
      Two real symptoms this cured:
        - a Wizard in seat 2+ NEVER got a spellbook. The 3 Fire Ball / 3 Lightning / 2 Teleport
          grant ran once on the working globals AFTER SetupPlayers, so it only ever landed on
          whoever was active at init (player 1). It is now granted per Wizard SEAT in SetupPlayers.
        - potions/XP/poison bled across seats (drink on your turn, the next player is short).
      `dungeon.run savetest` phase 0 proves the isolation by parking and restoring two seats with
      distinct kit; reverting the fix makes it fail with the exact player-visible symptoms.
      NOTE: `loiter` (lingering-danger meter) and `curio_cool` stay RUN-WIDE on purpose -- they
      read as "how restless the dungeon is", not as something a player carries.
    ☐ Tune the curio/trap/potion odds + saving-throw math against playtest feel (constants in DUNGEON.BI).
    ☐ Board legend art: add "$ = recoverable treasure" and a "fallen-body = an adventurer died here"
      marker to the baked .ans (art-side edit; the code already draws both via DrawEntities).

